{"author":"Unknown","author_email":"","data":{"advisory":[{"agreement":1,"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Make `_request_as`'s admin-fallback password read `JIRA_DC_ADMIN_PASSWORD` (matching `_admin_request`/conftest `_request`) instead of the hardcoded \"admin\" literal.","criteria":["correctness","maintainability"],"decision":"advisory","evidence":["tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_transport.py:593: `user, password = basic_auth if basic_auth is not None else (_ADMIN_USER, \"admin\")`","tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_transport.py:468-469: `user = os.environ.get(\"JIRA_DC_ADMIN\", \"admin\")` / `password = os.environ.get(\"JIRA_DC_ADMIN_PASSWORD\", \"admin\")`","conftest.py:105: `user, password = basic_auth if basic_auth is not None else (_ADMIN_USER, _ADMIN_PASSWORD)` where `_ADMIN_PASSWORD = os.environ.get(\"JIRA_DC_ADMIN_PASSWORD\", \"admin\")`"],"finding":"`_request_as` hardcodes the admin password literal \"admin\" in its basic-auth fallback, diverging from `_admin_request` and conftest `_request`, which both read `JIRA_DC_ADMIN_PASSWORD`. In any instance with a non-default admin password, the user-creation POST and the cleanup DELETE (which use this fallback) will 401.","id":"0","impact":0.3,"location":"tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_transport.py:593","norm_id":"n9c38f1429a13b1f0","priority":0.3,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Replace `(_ADMIN_USER, \"admin\")` with `(_ADMIN_USER, os.environ.get(\"JIRA_DC_ADMIN_PASSWORD\", \"admin\"))`.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","respects_artifact_altitude